{
 "description": "Write-ahead coordination: declare planned work BEFORE acting so parallel agents dedupe. Returns DECLARED, REPLAYED, or a typed DUPLICATE naming the live winner (a DUPLICATE does not transfer ownership). Declare a write-ahead work intent BEFORE starting spontaneous work so every other session sees ownership immediately. Exactly one of three outcomes: DECLARED (you own the fresh head), REPLAYED (same key + identical payload), or DUPLICATE \u2014 a typed loser packet naming the live winner (adopt, wait, or escalate a proposal; never race).",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
